Project Overview:
The MP3 Tag Reader and Editor is a command-line application developed in C to read, display, and edit ID3 metadata stored in MP3 files.
ID3 is a metadata container used in conjunction with the MP3 audio file format. It allows information such as the title, artist, album, track number, and other information about the file
to be stored in the file itself. The version used here is ID3V2.

Features:
* View metadata stored in an MP3 file.
* Edit selected metadata fields.
* Validate command-line arguments.
* Verify the MP3 file and ID3 tag header before processing.
* Read frame IDs, frame sizes, and metadata from the file.
* Update text fields without changing the existing frame size, provided the new text fits within the available space.
* Display help instructions for supported operations.

ID3V2:
  * VERSION
      1. ID3v2.2
      2. ID3v2.3
      3. ID3v2.4  
  * ID3v2 header has 10 bytes, where,
      1. ID3v2/file identifier is "ID3"
      2. ID3v2 version is $03 00 (2, 3, or 4)
      3. ID3v2 flag occupies 1 byte 
      4. ID3v2 size is 4 bytes
  * ID3v2.3 or ID3v2.4 Frame header
      1. Frame ID $xx xx xx xx (Four bytes)
        -> TPE1 - Artist name
        -> TIT2 - Title / Song name
        -> TALB - Album
        -> TYER - Year
        -> TCON - Content type
        -> TCOM - Comment 
      2. Size $xx xx xx xx (Four bytes)
      3. Flags $xx xx (2 Bytes)

Prerequisites:
* knowledge of ID3 tags
* File I/O
* String Handling
* Pointers and structure
Steps:
* Compile the required file using gcc *.c
* Run the program by passing information through Command line argument
   1. To view please pass like: ./a.out -v mp3_file_name
   2. To edit please pass like: ./a.out -e -t/-a/-A/-m/-y/-c changing_text mp3_file_name
   3. To get help pass like: ./a.out --help
* View Operation:
    -> validate the command line argument of view.
    -> Open the specified MP3 file and validate the ID3 header and supported version.
    -> Read each frame ID and its size.
    -> Extract the corresponding metadata from the frame.
    -> Store the extracted details in a structure.
    -> Display the metadata in a readable format.
* Edit Operation:
    -> Validate the command line argument of edit.
    -> Identify the metadata field selected by the user.
    -> Locate the corresponding frame in the MP3 file.
    -> Read the existing frame size and encoding information.
    -> Check whether the new text fits within the existing frame.
    -> Write the updated text and fill any remaining space when required.
    -> Report whether the update succeeded.
* Help Operation:
    -> Display the available commands and explain how to view or edit MP3 metadata.
      1. -v -> to view mp3 file contents
      2. -e -> to edit mp3 file contents
        2.1      -t -> to edit song title
        2.2      -a -> to edit artist name
        2.3      -A -> to edit artist name
        2.4      -y -> to edit year
        2.5      -m -> to edit content
        2.6      -c -> to edit comment
Learnings and Challenges: 
* Reading and writing binary files using C file I/O functions.
* Locating specific frames within a binary file.
* Updating data at the correct file position.
* Understanding the ID3v2.3 header and frame structure.
* Reading four-byte frame sizes and combining individual bytes.
Conclusion
This project helped strengthen my understanding of C programming and binary file handling to implementing an MP3 metadata reader and editor.
